NHES.S1.12.1	Students apply ways to build strengths that help both individual and shared health.
NHES.S1.12.2	Students analyze how the parts of wellness connect to health results.
NHES.S1.12.3	Students evaluate behaviors for how well they prevent or cut down illness and injury.
NHES.S1.12.4	Students evaluate habits that support health, including care of ongoing conditions.
NHES.S1.12.5	Students examine how health information skills of people and of organizations shape health results.
NHES.S1.12.6	Students analyze how factors at many levels connect and together shape health results.
NHES.S1.12.7	Students analyze what helps and what gets in the way of various health behaviors.
NHES.S1.12.8	Students examine how confidence in one's ability and sense of risk change health behavior.
NHES.S1.12.9	Students analyze how getting to health care relates to overall wellness.
NHES.S2.12.1	Students judge how influences and behaviors act on each other and on well-being.
NHES.S2.12.2	Students assess how social conditions such as income and neighborhood shape behaviors, results and equity 
in health.
NHES.S2.12.3	Students appraise how factors from the personal to the environmental affect fairness in health.
NHES.S2.12.4	Students design plans to handle the influences on their health and wellness.
NHES.S2.12.5	Students use the resources available to them to manage influences on well-being.
NHES.S3.12.1	Students examine how easy it is to reach trusted adults, professionals and resources for wellness.
NHES.S3.12.2	Students study what opens or blocks access to trustworthy health information and services.
NHES.S3.12.3	Students rate health resources on accuracy, trustworthiness and availability.
NHES.S3.12.4	Students choose accurate, trustworthy health sources and services and use them.
NHES.S3.12.5	Students use approaches that push back on misinformation and deliberate disinformation.
NHES.S4.12.1	Students communicate effectively through many channels and media to support well-being.
NHES.S4.12.2	Students use communication skills across many kinds of relationships and exchanges.
NHES.S4.12.3	Students show how to ask for and give help for health.
NHES.S4.12.4	Students use skills to state limits, give or take back consent, and set boundaries in varied situations.
NHES.S4.12.5	Students use ways to say no across different circumstances.
NHES.S4.12.6	Students use methods to prevent, manage and settle conflicts.
NHES.S4.12.7	Students show skills for working as a team in many settings.
NHES.S4.12.8	Students show negotiation and compromise skills in different settings.
NHES.S4.12.9	Students change how they communicate to suit people with other views and values.
NHES.S4.12.10	Students express understanding and concern for other people.
NHES.S5.12.1	Students consider how health decisions look to different people and communities.
NHES.S5.12.2	Students determine when and why a health situation needs a careful decision process.
NHES.S5.12.3	Students use a process done alone, with support or in a group to stay healthy.
NHES.S5.12.4	Students weigh the options against their priorities and likely results.
NHES.S5.12.5	Students examine how a decision could affect health at several levels.
NHES.S5.12.6	Students create an action plan for carrying out a health decision.
NHES.S5.12.7	Students judge how supports and barriers shape decisions at various levels.
NHES.S5.12.8	Students measure how well their health decisions worked.
NHES.S6.12.1	Students assess their own health and the factors that bear on pursuing a goal.
NHES.S6.12.2	Students use a goal process done alone, with support or together, whichever fits.
NHES.S6.12.3	Students write a goal and analyze how it supports health and well-being.
NHES.S6.12.4	Students carry out a plan that deals with supports and barriers.
NHES.S6.12.5	Students monitor progress and revise the goal or plan when needed.
NHES.S6.12.6	Students evaluate how the goal process went and what it did for health.
NHES.S7.12.1	Students assess what makes healthy behaviors easier or harder.
NHES.S7.12.2	Students judge how habits and other factors support wellness for people and groups.
NHES.S7.12.3	Students change habits as personal and group wellness needs change.
NHES.S7.12.4	Students show a range of habits that support the wellness of people and groups.
NHES.S8.12.1	Students study the many factors that shape advocacy at every level of life.
NHES.S8.12.2	Students take up a health issue, alone or with others.
