ent, watched; conduct: supports a partner's chosen activity without ranking it, S3.12.3 review, marked apart), 1 respond day. Product: the plan drafted on day 9, written teacher feedback, revised on day 11, scored at the check | Last in grade 10 because it gathers the required years into the plan every student leaves with; it needs unit 8's plan skills and the year's activities as choices | Candidate: the plan reused, unscored, as the first page of grade 11's program | Emotions: calm steps offered, never a punishment; a student may step out for a reset with a role; PE does not treat mental health conditions; the teacher page names the school counselor. Money and access: no student's family means are asked; options listed are free or low cost. Yoga as stretching and breathing, with no spiritual practice. Sensitivity read sources: the federal physical activity guidelines' adult pages; the national mental health institute's pages on stress and activity. Cost: $0 |
329:| 18 | 11 | Healthy and mine. *How do I find activity that improves my health and matches what I like?* | 10 | g11-health-interests | None owned | Cues: "health part, interest, match". Settings: sampling stations, then the student's matched activity in class | Finds and joins an activity that improves health and one that matches interests, and explains the match: used in new settings, SHAPE.S4.12.3 and SHAPE.S4.12.4 (grade 10, unit 12). Opens with retrieval on unit 16's program and grade 10 unit 12's plan. Ends: 1 check day (skill task: the matched activity's main cue; knowledge task: a short written reason for each choice; conduct: encourages a partner, S3.12.3 review), 1 respond day | Last in grade 11, closing the elective year with the student's own match, which grade 12's goals build on | Candidate: a "match card" kept for grade 12 | Health talk stays on activity, never body size. Emotions: calm steps offered; the teacher page names the school counselor. Cost: $0 |
332:| 21 | 12 | Steady in hard moments. *What helps me manage stress and strong feelings when I am active?* | 8 | g12-manage-emotions | None owned | Cues: breath work, pacing, a reset break, movement for stress; calm-steps. Settings: in-class sessions with a hard moment built in (a timed challenge, a new skill, a close game) | Examines and uses chosen ways to manage emotions during activity, breath work, pacing, a short break, movement for stress, and uses one in a hard moment: used in a new setting, SHAPE.S4.12.8 (grade 10, unit 12). Opens with retrieval on grade 11 unit 15's fitting challenge and on SEL 9 to 12 unit 20's response plan (weeks 6 to 11, just before); readiness check on grade 10 unit 12's emotion strategy in the last ten minutes of unit 20's respond day. Ends: 1 check day (knowledge task: a chosen method and why; conduct: the method used in a hard moment, watched; skill task: the session's main cue kept under pressure), 1 respond day | Short because it is one row; before the mid-year check so the check can sample S4 in grade 12 | Candidate: a pocket card of the student's own method | Emotions: no right answers; a student may step out for a reset with a role; PE does not treat mental health conditions; the teacher page names the school counselor and carries health's disclosure steps. Sensitivity read sources: the national mental health institute's pages on stress; SEL 9 to 12 unit 20's self-management words (Cross-subject). Cost: $0 |
335:| 24 | 12 | Looking back. *What has physical education meant to me, and what will I carry on?* | 10 | g12-reflect | None owned | Cues: "two examples, what it meant, what next". Settings: favorite-activity sessions chosen by the class, beside portfolio days | Thinks over PE experiences across the years to understand what they mean to the student, as a portfolio piece with two examples: used in a new setting, SHAPE.S4.12.9 (grade 10, unit 12). Each day opens with a chosen activity session, so the unit stays moving. Opens with retrieval on grade 11 unit 17 (a student without grade 11 gets a readiness check on grade 10 unit 12's reflection in the last ten minutes of the year-end respond day, day 70, before unit 24 opens). Ends: 1 check day (knowledge task: the reflection, drafted with written feedback and revised; skill task: the chosen activity's main cue; conduct: courtesy in the chosen session, S3.12.2 review), 1 respond day. The short form is in Grade 12 calendar | Last in the course, after the year-end check (week 28), so a senior who leaves early has finished the check; it closes the band | Candidate: a letter to a grade 9 student about PE | Emotions: reflections may touch hard experiences in PE; no student is asked to share aloud; the teacher page names the school counselor and carries health's disclosure steps. Cost: $0 |
