### Science and mathematics

No row of this course leans on a core science or math course (the rows' cross_subject cells name only ELA). Biology
runs the same year; health states its plain facts (infection, vaccines, condition care) itself, with their source
(STANDARD.md section 8), and reteaches no biology model. Number work stays inside what grades 6 and 7 math teach:
rates and percents in units 2, 3, 11 and 12, unit prices in unit 14, counts and a simple bar chart in unit 15.

## For the lead

1. **Semester term (pick: fall).** data/plans/course-list.csv has `term` `year` for health-grades-9-to-12, so
   `frame.py sync` spreads its 80 days over 32 weeks (about every other school day) and calendar.csv shows this
   course's checks near weeks 14 and 32. The course is one semester (STANDARD.md section 1, Desk q-fix-health-1):
   set `term` to `fall`, as for US Government and Politics, so days 1 to 80 fall on school weeks 1 to 16 and the
   checks on weeks 7 and 16 as this frame says. Then re-run sync.
2. **Dose (kept: 80 days of 45 minutes, 60 hours).** The national figure is 80 hours; a school that adds time adds
   days to units, never a new unit, and the goal slots stay weekly.
3. **Row change made.** g9-pa-measure-decisions gains `~NHES.S6.12.5` and a note line, so standard 6 is practiced in
   two topics with the sensitive rows out (pilot pattern note 1; Codex finding 3 of the pilot read).
   `progression.py check health` passes.
4. **Neighbor unit numbers.** This frame names the rows of health grades 6 to 8, PE grades 9 to 12 and SEL grades 9
   to 12, not their units. Pick: the lead's seam read adds their unit numbers to Seams and Cross-subject; the
   handoff cells agree at both ends, so no row changes.
5. **Supplies ceiling (money, Cory's).** $68 printing for a class of 30 a semester, $113 with the optional no-cook
   demonstration. Pick: $70 a semester, the demonstration outside it.
